The trusted translator reproduces `solution.mpy` byte-for-byte. An independent 12,126-case ASCII differential, including all strings through length four and long randomized lists, found zero contract-domain mismatches. It also exposed the expected underdetermined Unicode edge: the candidate treats Unicode numerals as non-odd while canonical often parses them numerically; I’ll account for that separately from the ASCII theorem.

The `validating-proof` workflow now requires a clean live replay and later a fresh false-result mutation. I’m compiling only from the scratch source copy.
